title: Walk_Heim_Socrates
tags: walk
speaker: Heim
---
Heim: We are returning down the forest path toward Socrates' clearing.
Heim: You have wrestled with virtual realism, digital objects, and the nature of existence.
Heim: Sunlight cuts through the tall canopy onto the dirt path.
Heim: Technology challenges us to refine our definition of what is genuine.
Heim: A virtual world is not a void; it contains structured information and real effects.
Heim: Socrates waits under his tree to review your conclusions.
Heim: Tell him whether you view digital landscapes as real entities or mere illusions.
Heim: Every distinction we draw helps illuminate the structure of reality.
Heim: Keep your mind sharp as we rejoin the central gathering.
Heim: Socrates will be ready for your final report.
===
